# Web security feature catalog for the acceptance report.
# area | feature | evidence
# evidence = comma-separated test names (all must pass), or
#            GAP: <why>  (not implemented / not verified — counted against completeness)
#            N/A: <why>  (does not apply)
#
# Covers kernway-http (the HTTP/1.1 codec), kernway-server (the server and its
# security middleware) and kernway-security (passwords, tokens, sessions, bans).
# The attack tests start a real Kernway server on a loopback port and send it
# raw bytes — what an attacker controls. Session, presence and ban stores run
# against a real Redis as well as in memory and on disk.

Request smuggling | Conflicting, repeated-but-different, signed, hex, negative or non-numeric Content-Length refused (400) | request_smuggling_vectors_are_refused_and_nothing_behind_them_runs, parser::byte_parser_tests::rfc_9112_framing_rules_are_enforced
Request smuggling | Transfer-Encoding together with Content-Length refused; a coding other than chunked refused (501); Transfer-Encoding in HTTP/1.0 refused | request_smuggling_vectors_are_refused_and_nothing_behind_them_runs
Request smuggling | Whitespace before a header's colon, obsolete line folding, control characters (NUL, bare CR), names that are not tokens, lines without a colon refused | request_smuggling_vectors_are_refused_and_nothing_behind_them_runs, parser::byte_parser_tests::rfc_9112_framing_rules_are_enforced
Request smuggling | Two Host headers refused; HTTP/2+ versions answered 505; malformed request lines refused | request_smuggling_vectors_are_refused_and_nothing_behind_them_runs, parser::byte_parser_tests::a_malformed_request_line_is_an_error_not_a_hang
Request smuggling | After a refusal the connection closes: the request hidden behind it never reaches a handler | request_smuggling_vectors_are_refused_and_nothing_behind_them_runs
Request smuggling | An HTTP/1.1 request without Host is refused (RFC 9112 §3.2) | GAP: accepted, as before (requests typed by hand rely on it); two Host headers are refused
Framing | Chunked request bodies decoded (extensions, trailers); the next pipelined request stays in step; equal Content-Length repeats accepted | chunked_request_bodies_are_decoded_and_the_next_request_stays_in_step, chunked::tests::bodies_trailers_and_what_follows, chunked::tests::broken_framing_is_refused
Framing | Pipelined requests answered in order; keep-alive limits; HTTP/1.0 closes by default | pipelined_requests_are_answered_in_order, app::keep_alive_tests::pipelined_requests_in_one_packet_are_both_answered, app::keep_alive_tests::max_requests_closes_the_connection_even_if_the_client_wants_more, app::keep_alive_tests::an_http10_client_gets_a_closed_connection_by_default
Response splitting | CR / LF / NUL a handler puts in a header value cannot end the header (folded to spaces); header names that are not tokens dropped; the transport owns Connection / Content-Length | a_header_built_from_user_input_cannot_split_the_response, writer::splitting_tests::a_header_value_cannot_split_the_response, writer::connection_tests::a_handler_cannot_override_the_connection_header

Resource limits | A head over 8 KiB refused (431) without buffering it; a body over max_upload_size refused (413) before it is read; a chunked upload past the ceiling stopped mid-way | oversized_heads_and_bodies_are_refused_before_they_are_read, a_large_chunked_upload_is_spooled_and_one_past_the_ceiling_refused, parser::byte_parser_tests::a_head_that_never_ends_is_rejected_rather_than_buffered_forever, app::tests::an_upload_over_the_ceiling_is_refused_with_413
Resource limits | Large bodies (Content-Length or chunked) spooled to disk, not memory | a_large_chunked_upload_is_spooled_and_one_past_the_ceiling_refused, app::tests::a_large_body_spools_to_disk_not_memory
Resource limits | Slow clients (slowloris) cut off at the idle timeout without an answer | a_slow_client_is_cut_off_at_the_idle_timeout, app::keep_alive_tests::an_idle_connection_is_closed_after_the_timeout
Resource limits | Request floods slowed with 429 per client; a forged X-Forwarded-For does not escape the limit; repeat offenders banned | a_flood_from_one_client_is_slowed_down, a_forged_x_forwarded_for_does_not_escape_the_rate_limit, rate_limit::tests::escalates_to_a_ban_after_repeated_violations, rate_limit::tests::separate_clients_have_separate_buckets
Resource limits | Client IP behind proxies: X-Forwarded-For trusted only from configured proxies; a spoofed left-hand entry defeated | tracking::tests::a_direct_client_uses_the_peer_and_ignores_forwarded_headers, tracking::tests::a_spoofed_left_hand_entry_is_defeated, tracking::tests::behind_a_trusted_proxy_uses_the_forwarded_client

Static files | Traversal refused: ../, percent-encoded (%2e%2e, %2f, %5c), double-encoded, backslashes, NUL, and a symlink out of the root | static_files_never_leave_their_root, app::static_file_tests::a_traversal_attempt_over_http_is_a_404, app::static_file_tests::a_symlink_escaping_the_root_is_rejected

Headers | Security headers on every response, errors included: nosniff, frame options, referrer policy, CSP, HSTS | security_headers_are_on_every_response, security::tests::security_headers_middleware_adds_headers_to_every_response, tests::strict_headers_have_the_secure_baseline
Headers | Cross-origin isolation (COOP / COEP / CORP) | cross_origin::tests::adds_isolation_headers_to_a_normal_response, cross_origin::tests::handler_set_headers_are_neither_overridden_nor_duplicated
CORS | Only listed origins are granted (lookalike, suffix, scheme and null origins refused); credentials never with a wildcard; Vary: Origin; a refused preflight grants nothing | cross_origin_reads_are_granted_only_to_listed_origins, cors::tests::credentials_echo_the_origin_never_wildcard, cors::tests::a_disallowed_origin_gets_no_cors_headers, app::tests::a_cors_preflight_is_answered_by_cors_never_by_the_router

CSRF | Every POST / PUT / PATCH / DELETE needs the token back (form field or header) — a forged cross-site write with the victim's cookie is refused (403); API calls with Authorization and exempt webhooks pass | forged_cross_site_writes_are_refused
CSRF | Tokens: 256-bit random, compared in constant time; cookie HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax (Secure over HTTPS); templates add the hidden field to every state-changing form | tests::a_token_is_64_hex_chars_and_unpredictable, tests::verify_is_exact, tests::the_cookie_is_httponly_and_samesite, tests::verify_request_matches_cookie_against_header_or_form

Authentication | JWT (HS256): signature checked first in constant time; alg none, alg confusion (RS256 header), a tampered payload, another key, expiry, not-before, issuer and audience refused | only_valid_tokens_with_the_right_role_get_in, jwt::tests::the_alg_none_attack_is_refused, jwt::tests::a_tampered_payload_is_rejected, jwt::tests::a_wrong_secret_is_rejected, jwt::tests::an_expired_token_is_rejected, jwt::tests::a_not_yet_valid_token_is_rejected, jwt::tests::issuer_and_audience_are_checked_when_expected, jwt::tests::malformed_tokens_are_rejected
Authentication | JWT (RS256) against a JWKS: tampering, a wrong issuer and an unknown key refused | jwt::tests::verifies_an_rs256_token_against_a_jwks, jwt::tests::rs256_rejects_tampering_wrong_issuer_and_unknown_key
Authentication | Tokens without exp never expire (no "require exp" setting) | GAP: not implemented — issue tokens with exp
Authentication | Sessions: forged and expired tokens anonymous; idle and absolute timeouts; logout everywhere; a version bump, a deactivated account or an expired subscription logs out; a session cap; the store down fails closed | session::tests::a_forged_token_is_anonymous, session::tests::an_expired_token_is_anonymous, session::tests::the_idle_timeout_logs_out_an_inactive_session, session::tests::the_absolute_timeout_is_enforced_live, session::tests::logout_user_kills_every_device, session::tests::a_version_bump_forces_re_login, session::tests::a_deactivated_account_is_logged_out, session::tests::max_sessions_refuses_a_new_login, session::tests::authenticate_fails_closed_when_the_store_is_down
Authentication | The same session rules against a real Redis, and across a restart on disk | session::tests::redis_seam::idle_timeout_logs_out_over_redis, session::tests::redis_seam::absolute_timeout_logs_out_over_redis, session::tests::redis_seam::version_bump_logs_out_over_redis, redis::login_flow_redis, redis::logout_user_over_redis, file_sessions::tests::logout_everywhere_survives_a_restart, file_sessions::tests::sessions_and_touches_survive_a_restart
Authentication | Passwords: PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 matching published vectors, salted (the same password hashes differently), self-describing so the cost can rise; bcrypt ($2a$) verified against jBCrypt vectors | password::tests::matches_published_pbkdf2_hmac_sha256_vectors, password::tests::the_same_password_hashes_differently_each_time, password::tests::a_hash_stays_verifiable_regardless_of_the_default_changing, password::tests::malformed_stored_strings_are_rejected_not_panicked, bcrypt::tests::verifies_canonical_jbcrypt_vectors, bcrypt::tests::rejects_wrong_password
Authentication | Login throttling: lockout after repeated failures, per key, expiring | lockout::tests::locks_out_after_the_threshold, lockout::tests::separate_keys_are_independent, lockout::tests::the_lock_expires, lockout::tests::a_success_clears_the_count
Authentication | Argon2 / scrypt password hashes; WebAuthn / TOTP second factors | GAP: not implemented

Authorization | Central path rules: unauthenticated → 401 (or a login redirect), wrong role → 403, first match wins, method-aware, authorities as well as roles | only_valid_tokens_with_the_right_role_get_in, security::tests::the_layer_allows_challenges_and_forbids_through_the_chain, security::tests::first_matching_rule_wins_then_the_default, security::tests::method_aware_rules_match_the_method, security::tests::decisions_cover_authority_axis, security::tests::login_page_redirects_anonymous_instead_of_401

Crypto | SHA-256 / HMAC-SHA256 match FIPS 180 and RFC 4231 vectors; secretbox (AEAD) refuses tampering, a wrong key, wrong associated data and a truncated tag | hash::tests::sha256_abc, hash::tests::hmac_rfc4231_case1, hash::tests::hmac_rfc4231_case2, secretbox::tests::tamper_fails, secretbox::tests::wrong_key_fails, secretbox::tests::wrong_aad_fails, secretbox::tests::truncated_tag_fails, secretbox::tests::nonce_makes_ciphertext_unique
Bans | IP, subnet (v4 and v6), User-Agent and principal bans; persisted on disk and in Redis across restarts | tracking::tests::bans_by_ip_subnet_and_user_agent, tracking::tests::ipv6_subnet_matching, tracking::tests::bans_a_principal_by_exact_match, file_bans::tests::bans_survive_a_restart_on_disk, bans_survive_a_restart

